"title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T11:55:09-07:00","id":1223972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1223968#post1223968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is extensive. It's going to take me a while to sit down and read through it all, but wow. This is every bit as awesome as I hoped it would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Shiunesh are our longest so far. All the others are in the realm of ca. 40-50 pages. Haven't thought about that before ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T18:25:56-07:00","id":1224040,"title":"","content":"I am very glad people are enjoying them! If anyone has any questions about them, myself and Sacerdos are always around. We hope people have fun reading about them, and learn a bit! Let us know how they go in your games if you wind up using them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T20:58:38-07:00","id":1224069,"title":"","content":"Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait. Did you just dance around the whole multiple Enkis thing by using an alternative romanization for Ea? That is hilarious and awesome and ballsy and I'm kinda embarrassed that it took more than thirty pages for me to catch on. In other news, I adore this, thank you so much. A couple of things though; I think Kumarbi's creature entry was cut off, an you seem to switch between Istanu and Ishantu with no pattern that I could see. Also, may I suggest a sidebar that makes it clear that the War God (who gets mentioned a couple of times) and other, similarly referred to deities are gods that we just don't know anything about? As is, it kind of comes off as an error by the final writer/editor. Thanks a bunch again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T21:19:05-07:00","id":1224073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1224069#post1224069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait. Did you just dance around the whole multiple Enkis thing by using an alternative romanization for Ea? That is hilarious and awesome and ballsy and I'm kinda embarrassed that it took more than thirty pages for me to catch on. In other news, I adore this, thank you so much. A couple of things though; I think Kumarbi's creature entry was cut off, an you seem to switch between Istanu and Ishantu with no pattern that I could see. Also, may I suggest a sidebar that makes it clear that the War God (who gets mentioned a couple of times) and other, similarly referred to deities are gods that we just don't know anything about? As is, it kind of comes off as an error by the final writer/editor. Thanks a bunch again</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less that we are skipping around the multiple Enkis as that modern Hittite scholarship uses Ea to refer to the entity we lack a proper Hittite name for. The Hittites were kings at adapting things, and took a lot of Sumerograms and used them for their own religious systems. We are just following the example of modern scholarship there since it helps prevent a <i>lot</i> of confusion since Hittite scholars work closely with Mesopotamian scholars. I don't want to claim credit for it, people who know the field far better than I do came up with it!<br /> <br /> Kumarbi's Creature section totally did get cut off, no clue how that happened, thanks for mentioning it! I'll fix it right away. And, yeah, the 'X Gods' are generally ones we know nothing about. I was intentionally leaving it in to try to keep some of the original oddity of the texts, and knowledge we have of the Hittites, but if it was serving as a point of confusion I'll absolutely add in a sidebar talking about it in the Nature of Divinity section. Thanks for pointing it out Center-of-All!<br /> <br /> I'm glad you're enjoying it as well! Always happy to see people having fun with what we produce, it really makes all the time and effort worth it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-02-2018, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T17:23:48-07:00","id":1224848,"title":"","content":"Do you guys think this Pantheon might look down on Scions born of humans more than others? If they think humans are nothing more than servants,even an Ascended one would have a hard time being accepted as a god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T17:38:47-07:00","id":1224853,"title":"","content":"My my...looks like I have something to read...(Presentation is well done)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T17:48:17-07:00","id":1224856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1224848#post1224848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys think this Pantheon might look down on Scions born of humans more than others? If they think humans are nothing more than servants,even an Ascended one would have a hard time being accepted as a god?</div> </div> </div> </div>While the \u0160iune\u0161 do have a... not-great relationship with humans, I don't think they will ever look down on Scions born of mortal and divine parentage sheerly for the fact of U\u0161\u1e2buni's existence. A powerful, sociopathic Titan who was a Scion originally. I think the Hittite Gods will never look down on mortal born Scions, but they might be very suspicious, and very cautious in their deals. U\u0161\u1e2buni was a Pantheon-Tier threat, and is the only half-divine Scion that existed from what we know, and thus similarly born Scions will have to find their way out from under his shadow and free themselves of suspicion.<br /> <br /> In general, the Scions of the Pantheon will be regarded as their servants first and foremost, a Scion will never find a loving child-parent or mentor relationship with the Hittite Gods (or Titans), there will always be this heavy division of expectation hanging over their heads.<br /> <br /> If a Scion manages to undergo Apotheosis who is not born from two deities or Created, they will be the first one to ascend in such a way. The Hittite Gods will likely find this to be an extreme curiosity, and might have different methods to 'purify' a Scion undergoing Apotheosis such as by using one of their jars to seal away their mortal nature. If a Scion of the Hittites favors mortals too heavily after their Apotheosis, they will again return to living in suspicion as one of the first Titans to overthrow Tarhun was similarly benevolent, though through his extreme sloth rather than actual kindness. (If a Scion wants to be benevolent, the best thing they can do is handle it on a case by case basis during prayers, arguing in favor of mortal plights in their courtroom style prayers, and trying to learn how to calm down the other deities from their rages)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T15:50:56-07:00","id":1225106,"title":"","content":"Some of the layout is a little off..(likely my Foxit pdf reader), and a few words aren't, <s><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">anathematic</span></s> should be anathema, but that's a bit nit-picky for something this well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T19:08:22-07:00","id":1225136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1225106#post1225106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the layout is a little off..(likely my Foxit pdf reader), and a few words aren't, <s><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">anathematic</span></s> should be anathema, but that's a bit nit-picky for something this well done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really sorry the layout is off! I haven't heard any complaints before, so it might be the reader? If you can PM me a screen shot I can compare it against what I have and let you know. If it is proving detrimental to reading it, maybe upload it to Google Drive?<br /> <br /> And thanks for the catch on the Bogovi bit. I spent a while milling it over, since I thought it made more sense grammatically to have an adjective after a form of To Be, but apparently this is one of those weird things about English!<br /> <br /> Have you enjoyed the Pantheon otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T12:24:58-07:00","id":1225402,"title":"","content":"I'll double check things over the weekend...but yeah this is good stuff!<br /> This particular pantheon seems to have similar attitudes with many of the Annunaki in regards with how humanity was treated. Although I dare say that the best humans could hope for in your \u0160iune\u0161 pantheon is indifference. (I like reading the differences and seeing some of the parallels)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:33:54-07:00","id":1239577,"title":"","content":"Well, now that I'm not trying to type on a Playstation, I can talk about this again. More thoughts and questions.<br /> <br /> 1. The setting material seems to imply that you presume worship in the Shiunesh is extinct or very nearly so, much moreso than implied for most pantheons in the new core. This seems especially blatant in the paragraph crossing pages 50 and 51. Was this divergence from the norm for this edition an intentional design choice on the part of your team, and if so, why did you make it? Or am I way off base?<br /> <br /> 2. Related to #1, if Shiunesh worship is so limited, why is Anatolia not an uninhabitable wasteland? This does not seem to be a pantheon that would take a lack of worship in good stride, and aside from that they're probably all hungry and smelly due to all the bathing and eating they're not doing as a result. Do you just assume that the Theoi/Yazatas/Tanrilar/whoever else I'm forgetting took up the slack (not with the eating/bathing, the other stuff)?<br /> <br /> 3. So, you evidently elected to put out this work solely in Scon 2e. Is it then reasonable to presume that Scion 2.0 is a functionally dead project, at least as a ruleset? What made you decide to go in this direction for your stuff?<br /> <br /> 4. A bit of a practical matter: how would you distinguish Tarhun from other thunderous god-kings in terms of characterization? I'm a bit under-educated on some of these, and struggle on how to keep him well-separated from figures like Marduk and especially Ba'al Hadad.<br /> <br /> 5. Is there anything interesting that you wound up cutting from the final pdf that you'd be interested in sharing or getting into more depth with?<br /> <br /> 6. I seem to recall that at one point, Watcher mentioned that both of the competing lineages in Hittite myth had both gods and titans in their ranks. This obviously changed at some point during the research and design process (unless I'm completely misremembering, or course). What compelled this change, and what figures had a different status in the earlier design?<br /> <br /> and lastly, how is progress going on your group's next project? I'm really eager to see whatever pantheon is next on the docket for you. Thank you very much for your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12989,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","user":"Center-of-All","date":". 07-28-2018, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T00:38:04-07:00","id":1239590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239577#post1239577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now that I'm not trying to type on a Playstation, I can talk about this again. More thoughts and questions.<br /> <br /> 1. The setting material seems to imply that you presume worship in the Shiunesh is extinct or very nearly so, much moreso than implied for most pantheons in the new core. This seems especially blatant in the paragraph crossing pages 50 and 51. Was this divergence from the norm for this edition an intentional design choice on the part of your team, and if so, why did you make it? Or am I way off base?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the author, but I'd guess because it's the best way to handle how little we know. We know more than we do about Gaulish paganism, but still very little here, compared to those traditions reimagined as thriving and continuous in the setting.<br /> <br /> Personally I plan to up that even further and make the Shiunesh another dead pantheon like the Nemetondevos. Taking them down was something the Netjer, Elohim, Anunnaki, Yazatas, and Theoi were all actually able to agree on!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Related to #1, if Shiunesh worship is so limited, why is Anatolia not an uninhabitable wasteland? </div> </div> </div>As with the Nemetondevos being tied to their sacred shrines, seems that the Shiunesh are a pantheon who by virtue of being empowered by worship, by the same measure are screwed over by its absence. The nature of their PSP means that as their worship wanes, they have less muscle to bring to bare in response. (The Teotl are the other pantheon who run the risk of falling in this trap)<br /> <br /> That's assuming of course they aren't a dead pantheon like I intend at my own table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-28-2018, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T02:06:40-07:00","id":1239607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. The setting material seems to imply that you presume worship in the Shiunesh is extinct or very nearly so, much moreso than implied for most pantheons in the new core. This seems especially blatant in the paragraph crossing pages 50 and 51. Was this divergence from the norm for this edition an intentional design choice on the part of your team, and if so, why did you make it? Or am I way off base? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we personally prefer to set our Pantheons in the world as we ourselves live in it every day. We assume that reframing this in the context of Scion 2e's World is easy enough; generally, we make up as little as possible, so you can just take the source materials as they are, and reframe them whichever way you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Related to #1, if Shiunesh worship is so limited, why is Anatolia not an uninhabitable wasteland? This does not seem to be a pantheon that would take a lack of worship in good stride, and aside from that they're probably all hungry and smelly due to all the bathing and eating they're not doing as a result. Do you just assume that the Theoi/Yazatas/Tanrilar/whoever else I'm forgetting took up the slack (not with the eating/bathing, the other stuff)? </div> </div> </div>That is basically my assumption. On the one hand, some of the Shiunesh went on being worshipped under other names (mantles) for millennia, including the Minor Goddess Kubaba, who under her Mantle of Kybele became not only a Major member of the castration-happy Phrygian pantheon (worshipped outside Phrygia as well into Eastern Anatolia and Thrace), but later also, by sharing her Mantle with Rhea/Ops, one of the Theoi. On the other hand, the Theoi and Yazata did all the godly stuff in Anatolia for the rest of Antiquity, later being displaced by however Christianity and Islam work (I'm not getting into that!). So yeah, don't worry, Turkey is taken care of, at least in that respect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. So, you evidently elected to put out this work solely in Scon 2e. Is it then reasonable to presume that Scion 2.0 is a functionally dead project, at least as a ruleset? What made you decide to go in this direction for your stuff? </div> </div> </div>Short answer: Kinda. We elected to go with the times instead of constructing what would essentially have been an unnecessary rival product to 2e. We assume that the majority of people is going to switch to 2e anyway, and so this is where our work will be more useful. Long answer: I'll leave that to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. A bit of a practical matter: how would you distinguish Tarhun from other thunderous god-kings in terms of characterization? I'm a bit under-educated on some of these, and struggle on how to keep him well-separated from figures like Marduk and especially Ba'al Hadad. </div> </div> </div>Oh, while there's huge overlap in function, they're very easy to keep apart in character. Tarhun, to put it mildly, is a dick. He'll do anything to stay in power, he'll blast his own children to shreds, he'll lie, he'll cheat - he makes Zeus look like a saint. He's a very war-like god who'll have his bulls graze in the ruins of destroyed cities. He's a fitting leader to the generally very aggressive and very demanding Shiunesh.<br /> Ba'al Hadad is the young hero, a figure full of sexual vigour and youthful energy, a monster fighter and a dying-and-rising god. He's also struggling in a complicated web of politics where half the pantheon secretely or not-so-secretely wants him dead, and so sometimes he does paranoid things like refusing to have windows in his palace.<br /> With Marduk, you should never forget that he's a composite figure, who subsumes a lot of the associations of the older Mesopotamian storm gods Ishkur and Ninurta. He has very strong associations with Water and even stronger ones with kingship than the other two - him vacating his throne is an absolute disaster, where for the Elohim, it's kind of just the result of the &quot;scheme of the week&quot;. Thus, I'd characterise Marduk as quite haughty, even though he, too, is said to be of relatively lowly origins, having basically received his kingship as payment for defeating Tiamat. He's also definitely the most overpowered of the three, as the Royal Dynasties of Babylon just kept stuffing this their personal god with ever more attributes.<br /> So yeah, I think they're all quite easy to tell apart <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Is there anything interesting that you wound up cutting from the final pdf that you'd be interested in sharing or getting into more depth with? </div> </div> </div>Not really. As you can tell from the length of this, we don't really do cuts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> At one point, I suggested doing a little Appendix on what became of the Hurrian Mantles of the Shiunesh in the later Armenian Empire of Urartu, but that never got off the ground for reasons of lack of sources on those guys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. I seem to recall that at one point, Watcher mentioned that both of the competing lineages in Hittite myth had both gods and titans in their ranks. This obviously changed at some point during the research and design process (unless I'm completely misremembering, or course). What compelled this change, and what figures had a different status in the earlier design? </div> </div> </div>Hm, that might have been before we clearly settled on 2e? Or might have been miscommunication? Because one line <i>has</i> to be Titans, for the reason already that Titan is such a political designation for &quot;enemy&quot;. However, both sides have various Primordials on their side, so that might be where the confusion comes from? Anu and Aya side with Tarhun, Alalu and his folks with Kumarbi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and lastly, how is progress going on your group's next project? I'm really eager to see whatever pantheon is next on the docket for you. </div> </div> </div>One pantheon is currently going through the last bits of proof-reading and should hopefully be ready to go soon. Two are still having their PSPs meddled with to make them easier to implement. And two are currently being researched and written, and promise to take a whole lot more time, because I swear, sources on the Ta\u00edno just want to make me sad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you very much for your time. </div> </div> </div>You're welcome! We're always happy to answer questions on our projects! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T07:43:18-07:00","id":1239676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239577#post1239577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The setting material seems to imply that you presume worship in the Shiunesh is extinct or very nearly so, much moreso than implied for most pantheons in the new core. This seems especially blatant in the paragraph crossing pages 50 and 51. Was this divergence from the norm for this edition an intentional design choice on the part of your team, and if so, why did you make it? Or am I way off base?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what Sacerdos said. I don't use The World in my games, and I find it is easier for people to take historic perspectives and modernize them than being given modernized versions and need to work backwards. By presenting ancient and un-modernized Deities, we can service both people who want to modernize the Pantheons, as well as people who want to keep them as they were. The Pantheon can be easily converted to any setting with this base level of knowledge, rather than causing a telephone problem of people basing their reinterpretation off a reinterpretation.<br /> <br /> As you can expect, someone who is as twichy about being accurate as I am, and spends way too much time making Scion 'work,' doesn't use The World. It's just not the setting I find fun for Scion, and I have already spent an inordinate amount of time making a setting that I enjoy as I've talked on the forums about before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239577#post1239577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Related to #1, if Shiunesh worship is so limited, why is Anatolia not an uninhabitable wasteland? This does not seem to be a pantheon that would take a lack of worship in good stride, and aside from that they're probably all hungry and smelly due to all the bathing and eating they're not doing as a result. Do you just assume that the Theoi/Yazatas/Tanrilar/whoever else I'm forgetting took up the slack (not with the eating/bathing, the other stuff)?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a particularly tricky situation that exists for the Anunna as well, it just tends to be glossed over in representations of them. Different Storyguides will want to explain this situation in different ways, so we intentionally gave people the information, and let them devise a reality that fits whatever game they want to play. The other Pantheons that existed in Anatolia such as the Nemetondevos (everyone always forgets the Galatians!) probably took over managing things as the Shiunesh faded into the background, but as Sacerdos says, some of them stuck around in forms that are familiar to us in the modern world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239577#post1239577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. So, you evidently elected to put out this work solely in Scon 2e. Is it then reasonable to presume that Scion 2.0 is a functionally dead project, at least as a ruleset? What made you decide to go in this direction for your stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that Scion 2.0 is dead or over, we are just currently watching and deciding which direction we want to focus ourselves. I wanted to write a Pantheon for 2e to experiment with the system and learn more about it. I also wanted to give people some more Pantheons to play with in 2e, so, myself and Sacerdos put out a Pantheon for 2e. We have not decided which system is better suited for our groups games, but as we play more with both, we'll come to a decision.<br /> <br /> 4. A bit of a practical matter: how would you distinguish Tarhun from other thunderous god-kings in terms of characterization? I'm a bit under-educated on some of these, and struggle on how to <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239577#post1239577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">keep him well-separated from figures like Marduk and especially Ba'al Hadad.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Sacerdos said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239577#post1239577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. Is there anything interesting that you wound up cutting from the final pdf that you'd be interested in sharing or getting into more depth with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... I think everything that went pen to paper wound up in there. There were less Primordials originally until we just added the rest of the known Primeval Gods, but that's the opposite of things being cut.<br /> <br /> Oh and there was a different version of the PsP that was just horrible that Iry fixed. I'm slowly getting better at writing PsPs, but they'll always be the bane of me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239577#post1239577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. I seem to recall that at one point, Watcher mentioned that both of the competing lineages in Hittite myth had both gods and titans in their ranks. This obviously changed at some point during the research and design process (unless I'm completely misremembering, or course). What compelled this change, and what figures had a different status in the earlier design?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so, I may have explained this badly.<br /> <br /> Both factions of the Pantheon could be Gods and Titans is what I meant. The deciding factor of Titanhood for the Hittites is the opposition to the King, so, whichever faction is currently the ruling authority are Gods, whichever faction is the rebellious aggressors are Titans. So, it's less that one faction is comprised of both Gods and Titans, but both factions could be Gods or Titans depending on which one holds political authority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239577#post1239577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and lastly, how is progress going on your group's next project? I'm really eager to see whatever pantheon is next on the docket for you. Thank you very much for your time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pantheons are going pretty well, I need to work on some PsPs, but the next one is sort of in editing. I also have a 150 page expansion for the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann that's in editing at the moment, just cleaning up the last 50 pages of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T10:49:50-07:00","id":1239732,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for your responses. Always wonderful to hear more about your stuff. I actually came up with something else after sleeping on it, but I was wondering if your standards of assessment for purviews and gods has changed at all recently in reaction to 2e? A bit of a comparison between your 2.0 TtD and the official pantheon for 2e pretty clearly shows that you had much more exacting standards as to what constitutes a major member of a pantheon, and as to what constitutes sufficient evidence for a purview being associated. Did 2e's looser criteria influence your own considerations on this or future projects?<br /> <br /> And another thing, because I apparently can't keep my thoughts ordered today. Would any of the Shiunesh titans or primordials happen to fit into the Danu/Kitchi-Manitou category of &quot;not strictly a god, but still fit for divine parenthood anyway?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T13:20:50-07:00","id":1239780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239732#post1239732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very much for your responses. Always wonderful to hear more about your stuff. I actually came up with something else after sleeping on it, but I was wondering if your standards of assessment for purviews and gods has changed at all recently in reaction to 2e? A bit of a comparison between your 2.0 TtD and the official pantheon for 2e pretty clearly shows that you had much more exacting standards as to what constitutes a major member of a pantheon, and as to what constitutes sufficient evidence for a purview being associated. Did 2e's looser criteria influence your own considerations on this or future projects?<br /> <br /> And another thing, because I apparently can't keep my thoughts ordered today. Would any of the Shiunesh titans or primordials happen to fit into the Danu/Kitchi-Manitou category of &quot;not strictly a god, but still fit for divine parenthood anyway?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>We are always more than happy to answer questions on anything we produce!<br /> <br /> Our standards for Purviews and Gods has not changed going into 2e, the biggest change in that area is the dividing of Titans into Titans and Primordials. Our standard for what 'is' a God obviously changes from Pantheon to Pantheon, and the 'bar' for having a Purview or Calling changes similarly. We intend to allow each individual culture define themselves rather than forcefully fit them into different pan-Pantheon standards. We haven't changed to a looser standard for this or for future projects, and we intend to keep our little explanations for each Calling and Purview so people know why we made certain decisions.<br /> <br /> In areas we will deviate from RAW, for instance, several of the new members of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann I have written have less than the standard 3 Callings and 3 Purviews simply because they are hyper-minor characters I am including mostly for the completion of the \u00e1es d\u00e1na section of Cath Maige Tuired.<br /> <br /> The Primeval Gods (Hittite Primordials) by and large wouldn't work for Divine Parents as they are sealed away within The Dark Earth. The one exception is Aya who for some reason is still wandering around. The only issue about writing Aya up as a Divine Parent is that he is representative of a single concept: Knowledge. As Knowledge has no Purview (Him being an Order Primordial is a <i>big</i> stretch) he can't easily be made into a potential Divine Parent. If you really wanted him to be one, a Scion might inherit Sage from him, and <i>maybe</i> Order due to his Kingmaker role. Asides from that, he isn't representative of any other Purviews or Callings.<br /> <br /> When the rules for Titan Scions come out, Kumarbi would be a great potential Divine Parent, possibly Illuyanka as well!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T13:23:46-07:00","id":1239781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the rules for Titan Scions come out, Kumarbi would be a great potential Divine Parent, possibly Illuyanka as well! </div> </div> </div>Especially since Kumarbi <i>does</i> fuck around like nobody's business in mythology (like, he gets it on with a Giant Rock), and produces the only known Born Scion of the Shiunesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T21:12:48-07:00","id":1240712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1239732#post1239732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another thing, because I apparently can't keep my thoughts ordered today. Would any of the Shiunesh titans or primordials happen to fit into the Danu/Kitchi-Manitou category of &quot;not strictly a god, but still fit for divine parenthood anyway?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note, that doesn't seem to have stuck with Danu. She's not on the Pantheon list in Origin, while Kitchi-Manitou is. I think that's for the best as she's not an active presence in any surviving Irish myths, and the thematic role she potentially served as a divine patron is adequately (and more interestingly in my opinion) filled by Eriu as the Sovereignty Goddess of the land itself. Kitchi-Manitou is the ONLY Primordial it appears we're getting written up as a divine patron in the forseeable future - this also makes him more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T22:27:37-07:00","id":1240726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1240712#post1240712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to note, that doesn't seem to have stuck with Danu. She's not on the Pantheon list in Origin, while Kitchi-Manitou is. I think that's for the best as she's not an active presence in any surviving Irish myths, and the thematic role she potentially served as a divine patron is adequately (and more interestingly in my opinion) filled by Eriu as the Sovereignty Goddess of the land itself. Kitchi-Manitou is the ONLY Primordial it appears we're getting written up as a divine patron in the forseeable future - this also makes him more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not gonna say we've run away with that concept in our pantheons, but ... we kinda have XD The Shiunesh are pretty much our only pantheon that doesn't have at least two Primordials in it ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T09:20:35-07:00","id":1240907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1240712#post1240712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to note, that doesn't seem to have stuck with Danu. She's not on the Pantheon list in Origin, while Kitchi-Manitou is. I think that's for the best as she's not an active presence in any surviving Irish myths, and the thematic role she potentially served as a divine patron is adequately (and more interestingly in my opinion) filled by Eriu as the Sovereignty Goddess of the land itself. Kitchi-Manitou is the ONLY Primordial it appears we're getting written up as a divine patron in the forseeable future - this also makes him more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, we'll see. She wasn't in the Origins pantheon list in the Origins text-only preview, either, but she still had her stats in the Hero text preview. More damning, actually, is that Brahma and Xiwangmu, both of whom were in the text preview, are now no longer in evidence. Either way, those three would still be my top guesses for being the Companion additions for their respective pantheons.<br /> <br /> Also, another question! Would you have any Calling/Purview recommendations for anyone who wanted to go against your recommendations and run Kurunta as a divine parent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T19:06:17-07:00","id":1241115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1240907#post1240907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, another question! Would you have any Calling/Purview recommendations for anyone who wanted to go against your recommendations and run Kurunta as a divine parent?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first thing I would say is that it would be really beneficial to wait to get the Titan Callings that Neall has talked about to make a lot of these figures work as Divine Parents. However, if someone absolutely desperately wanted Kurunta as a Divine Parent right this instant, I would suggest the following: Hunter, Guardian, Warrior. Epic Dexterity, Prosperity, Wild.<br /> <br /> Now, I would suggest against Kurunta as a Divine Parent primarily due to his personality. He will abandon you, probably not give you any Birthrights, and I doubt he could even be bothered to Visit any of his Scions. Kurunta was so lazy as the King of the Gods that it was both self-destructive, and dangerous to the entire Pantheon. I really need to emphasize this since I think some people may read him as the 'One Good God' they have. He <i>really</i> is not. He just cares <i>so incredibly little</i> that he didn't enforce any of the rules of their cosmos, and he is so lazy he didn't do anything with his rule. Humanity may have benefited when he was King, but, a child of his would be left abandoned and never given any help or assistance. It isn't that he is malevolent, but he couldn't be bothered. He has already abandoned family before, and managed to attract the personal direct ire of a Primordial. He would possibly be the worst Divine Parent since even Visiting Scions is something I doubt he would ever do. He just <i>does not care</i> about anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T20:46:26-07:00","id":1241147,"title":"","content":"OK, that's fair, thank you. Seems like a pretty standard &quot;hunter god&quot; set with a sloth?-induced Prosperity thrown in.<br /> <br /> My question on the matter wasn't due to a &quot;One good god&quot; thing, that wasn't really the impression I got, but due to his rather strong cult. I figured that there must have been a reason he had one (people presumably either thought he'd help them in some way, or that he'd cause some sort of harm if they didn't; your write up of him does mention a protective function at a couple of points, and you're not going to guard something if you literally do not care one whit about it) and so there must have been some sort activity on Kurunta's part (he did care enough to fight for the throne, even if he didn't do anything with it, and also he presumably at least did some, y'know, hunting.) Honestly, most of your descriptions on the matter read to me less like laziness, per se, and more like apathy on the matter of his crown.<br /> <br /> Which actually gets me thinking, now. Do we actually know much about Hittite(/Hurrian/Lwian etc.) religious practices in specific? You mention the tribunal-prayers and the personal care given to proxies, and that the royal family has religious functions around the empire as one of its primary responsibilities, but little in the specific of the unique points of worshiping Telipinu vs Kamrusepa, or how Inara worship differed from Kurunta worship, or what it really meant, religiously, when Istanu overshadowed Tarhun in the captial. Is this something that we have any real information on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T21:01:26-07:00","id":1241152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1241147#post1241147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which actually gets me thinking, now. Do we actually know much about Hittite(/Hurrian/Lwian etc.) religious practices in specific? You mention the tribunal-prayers and the personal care given to proxies, and that the royal family has religious functions around the empire as one of its primary responsibilities, but little in the specific of the unique points of worshiping Telipinu vs Kamrusepa, or how Inara worship differed from Kurunta worship, or what it really meant, religiously, when Istanu overshadowed Tarhun in the captial. Is this something that we have any real information on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question! I will leave it for Sacerdos for the specifics since this is more his wheelhouse, but we know a fair amount of Hittite religious practices. We do not have a perfect picture (but that is not uncommon) but we have records of various religious laws, and recorded prayers being offered up to various Gods. From what I saw working through the translations of prayers I was working with, similarities existed in the worship of different Gods, but different things would be offered up to different Gods with different expectations for what a God could do.<br /> <br /> I think we <i>do</i> have some information on Istanu and Tarhun in the Capital, but I will leave it to Sacerdos. I can remember we had a long discussion about it at one point due to GBN using Istanu as the Pantheon Head. I believe it was an incredibly late, and short run situation, but Sacerdos will know more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T04:19:21-07:00","id":1241752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which actually gets me thinking, now. Do we actually know much about Hittite(/Hurrian/Lwian etc.) religious practices in specific? You mention the tribunal-prayers and the personal care given to proxies, and that the royal family has religious functions around the empire as one of its primary responsibilities, but little in the specific of the unique points of worshiping Telipinu vs Kamrusepa, or how Inara worship differed from Kurunta worship, or what it really meant, religiously, when Istanu overshadowed Tarhun in the captial. Is this something that we have any real information on? </div> </div> </div>Sorry for taking a while, but I've been crazy tired yesterday. Also sorry because I won't be able to give a super-good answer, because you're asking for something that requires a lot of detail, and it's been several years now since I read those specific details. We <i>do</i> have a lot on Hittite religion, more than on their mythology, actually, because they were wonderfully bureaucratic and wrote everything down. A problem, however, is that what we know has undergone a process of random selection due to which sources have been preserved and in what form. As a non-religious example that I like a lot: We have lots of Hittite treaties with other powers - but only in copy. We possess only one of the metal tablet originals, and that one only because it was buried as a curse instead of being honourably put in a temple, where all of the others were stolen and melted down after the fall of the empire. Our situation with religion is similar, in that we have no religious images, very few temples with more than the foundations left, and that a lot of the ritual instructions that tell us how stuff was done allude to lost materials. Because being bureaucratic also means not writing everything down twice but saying &quot;look over in folder F for this&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, what do we know about Hittite ritual, especially in regards to differences between the specific deities? Basically, the Hittites have a lot in common with the Kami or Shen in that regard - both in that ritual orthodoxy is immensely important for your prayers to reach the deity in question, and in that all deities are essentially local. Most of the deities we present in our write-up are already amalgamations of various linked local deities, and as you can see from the lists of aliases, these connections and syncretisations span several cultures. So every one of these complex deities has numerous local manifestations with miniscule differences - for example, we gave Tarhun Fertility for his Luwian form's associations with viniculture, which his Hittite and Hurrian forms entirely lack. And every one of those 'Mantles' has its own local cult with its own cultic tradition which <i>must be observed</i>. It doesn't work if you try to change things! (Of course things changed anyway, but the change was slow and not very deliberate compared to what was going on with constructed uber-gods like Marduk and Amun in the surrounding nations). This means that a deity's Hattian form had to be prayed to in the Hattian language, otherwise they wouldn't listen, even if at home in Hattussa the same deity was being worshipped in Hittite. Then, over several great state festivals, the royal couple would tour the entire country, visit all the major cult centres of all the ethnicities and religions in their realm, and participate in all those orthodox and incredibly variant rituals. Like I said, I can't give you a lot of details off the top of my head, but e.g. in Telipinu's ritual, a tree was planted, Ishhara's temple had a ritual bed for her priestess to be ritually married on, etc.<br /> <br /> Now, I think that covers your first question. As for the second one, the difference between Inara and Kurunta, that is more difficult. Inara's worship is mostly limited to the Old Kingdom of the Hittites, and becomes less and less prominent over time, whereas the male LAMMA-God (which you can associate with Kurunta). There's been a lot of debate in scholarly circles over whether they became actually conflated in Hittite times or not, and I can't give you a clear answer on that. If you want to look into the issue in more detail, though, there's a whole book on the LAMMA-Gods available online: <a href=\"https://oi.uchicago.edu/sites/oi.uchicago.edu/files/uploads/shared/docs/as25.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://oi.uchicago.edu/sites/oi.uch.../docs/as25.pdf</a><br /> <br /> As for Ishtanu and Tarhun, it's like Watcher said, our ideas of that are heavily skewed by the religious policies of Tudhaliya IV, one of the last known kings of the Hittites, who was a huge fan of Hurrian culture, built a huge and beautiful temple to the Hurrian gods (Yazilikaya), and just generally left us a lot of sources - a lot of them, but obviously not the most representative ones. The primacy of Ishtanu is basically derived from the importance of that god's equivalents among the Hurrians and Luwians, and from the association of him with Arinniti towards the end of the Hittite New Kingdom. But we tried to go with the older tradition that still put the Hittites' own interpretations of their gods in a more central position, and that interpretation, I think, was also in vogue far longer than Tudhaliya's policy of promoting Hurrian ideas and worshipping the Sun God of the Sky (and even at Yazilikaya, the Storm God takes the most prominent position, so there's that ...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T10:46:02-07:00","id":1241917,"title":"","content":"Oh, wow, that's actually really great. Thanks for the long explanation and the link, very much appreciated. I hope you're feeling a bit better now. Looks like<br /> I have a bit of reading ahead of me. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T11:31:54-07:00","id":1241943,"title":"","content":"How would you go about making a scion of Hahhima? Within my version of &quot;The World&quot; scions of the more inhuman Titans are definitely possible, there are scions of Apep and Fenrir running around, though how exactly said scions come into existence is something I haven't quite figured out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T11:40:28-07:00","id":1241949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1241943#post1241943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you go about making a scion of Hahhima? Within my version of &quot;The World&quot; scions of the more inhuman Titans are definitely possible, there are scions of Apep and Fenrir running around, though how exactly said scions come into existence is something I haven't quite figured out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahhima is a challenge as he is Omnipresent and lacks a body. He bridges the line between Primordial and Titan pretty heavily, but is too directly involved with the Pantheon in a major event to really be solidly a Primordial. Especially since the Hittites have a very specific division of what is and what is not a Primordial, and Hahhima does not fit into it.<br /> <br /> I would probably say that Hahhima cannot create Scions, or would have zero desire to do so. He is essentially the heat death of the universe, destroying everything, leaving reality static, and frozen to the absolute core. Everything stops. Having a Scion essentially goes directly against his very nature, as that Scion's existence would be directly opposed to Hahhima's core nature of static, immobile existence. If he did have a Scion, it would probably be either an entirely immobile and static object with a personality, or an incorporeal force similar to Hahhima. So, not really viable for a Player Character, but a decent antagonist I suppose.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if this isn't the answer you wanted. Hahhima is a step further than the animalistic Titans in inhumanity, Hahhima doesn't even have a body and exists everywhere at once. If you really-really wanted to have a Scion of his, I guess you could just use the normal rules. But, by and large, Hahhima has no desire or need to create Scions, and creating Scions goes against his fundamental nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-02-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T11:48:39-07:00","id":1241957,"title":"","content":"Okay. I was under the impression that he was at least capable of manifesting a physical form in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T11:56:31-07:00","id":1241960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1241957#post1241957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I was under the impression that he was at least capable of manifesting a physical form in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and that's what makes him so interesting! He has no body, no physical form, you cannot see him, or strike him. He is omnipresent as far as we can tell reading the story, but he does have a personality and voice. He taunts Tarhun as Tarhun dies along with the rest of the Pantheon from the overwhelming cold that has taken them, freezing them all in place in an instant. He has no corporeal form, and exists everywhere at once all the time.<br /> <br /> He is probably one of the more dangerous Titans across all of the Pantheons to be honest, he took down the entire Pantheon in the blink of the eye, and how he was defeated is forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T12:07:04-07:00","id":1241964,"title":"","content":"I absolutely love the Hittite Titans to be honest. I'm seriously toying with the idea of Ushhuni as being a monstrous threat to all the pantheons, a &quot;God-Butcher&quot; who hates all divinity and has murdered countless deities. He's a terrifying, badass, villain, and I'd love to use him as a big bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T12:12:36-07:00","id":1241973,"title":"","content":"Wait, wasn't that a plot in a Thor comic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T12:16:52-07:00","id":1241975,"title":"","content":"That is where I came up with the term &quot;God-Butcher.&quot; I could see Ushhuni having a similar role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T13:11:27-07:00","id":1242012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1241943#post1241943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you go about making a scion of Hahhima? Within my version of &quot;The World&quot; scions of the more inhuman Titans are definitely possible, there are scions of Apep and Fenrir running around, though how exactly said scions come into existence is something I haven't quite figured out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahhima isn't really inhuman in the way Apep and Fenrir are (they are because they are, in the end, huge animals), and more in the way that the Titanrealms of 1e were - he's more concept than person, an atmosphere, the cold and stagnation itself rather than its personification. So I'm gonna take the easy way out here and tell you: How would you make a Scion of that? The same way you'd get any other abstract concept to fuck a human. ^^'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","user":"Sacerdos","date":".  EDIT: Oh, whoops I missed that there was a third page already 08-02-2018, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T02:42:05-07:00","id":1242275,"title":"","content":"This is admittedly off-topic but still has to do with your project as a whole:<br /> <br /> Do you have any plans to write up the Kachinas? There's a fairly large demand for these guys, and they're my favorite First Nations pantheon, but nothing has been indicated officially one way or the other in regards to plans for their inclusion. Are they on your list? I cannot express strongly enough how much I want them in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T03:13:28-07:00","id":1242279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1242275#post1242275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is admittedly off-topic but still has to do with your project as a whole:<br /> <br /> Do you have any plans to write up the Kachinas? There's a fairly large demand for these guys, and they're my favorite First Nations pantheon, but nothing has been indicated officially one way or the other in regards to plans for their inclusion. Are they on your list? I cannot express strongly enough how much I want them in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've definitely discussed doing the Navajo/Dine Pantheon. I think they were talking about putting them in Demigod, but Neall recently informed us that the exact Pantheon makeup is under discussion right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T03:22:54-07:00","id":1242281,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm aware that the Navajo are being worked on. That's actually part of why I'd like to see a homebrew write-up for the Hopi, as I doubt they'll be officially doing a second southwestern First Nations pantheon any time soon. Still definitely happy to have the Navajo as well though. Plus, there are a huge number of Kachinas, and judging by the Shiunesh, space for the Watcher/Sacerdos write-ups is pretty much unlimited, which is totally awesome, so I'd like to see a fairly sizable roster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T10:41:46-07:00","id":1242421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1242275#post1242275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is admittedly off-topic but still has to do with your project as a whole:<br /> <br /> Do you have any plans to write up the Kachinas? There's a fairly large demand for these guys, and they're my favorite First Nations pantheon, but nothing has been indicated officially one way or the other in regards to plans for their inclusion. Are they on your list? I cannot express strongly enough how much I want them in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do not currently have any plans for the Kachinas, I didn't realize there was a large demand. If there is, we probably need to leave them to Onyx Path, our goal is to never directly cross over into the Pantheons they want to do. Instead, we are going after the more obscure Pantheons, or Pantheons that are rather difficult to do unless you are willing to break away from Scion's methedolody to create, such as Pantheons with less than five Gods, or Pantheons that are primarily Primordials, and the like.<br /> <br /> I am currently putting the finishing edits on my T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann expansion, and proof reading our next Pantheon. We have three Pantheons in a functional order at the moment, minus PsPs being up to par, a fourth I need to write the Cosmology for, a Fifth in mind that Sacerdos has thoroughly researched, and a potential sixth we were discussing yesterday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T11:35:31-07:00","id":1242442,"title":"","content":"Cool. I'm curious what Pantheon number seven might be. Any hints in terms of general world region?<br /> <br /> I didn't know you were writing an expansion to the Tuatha, but that's awesome, given your personal expertise on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T11:54:30-07:00","id":1242445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1242442#post1242442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. I'm curious what Pantheon number seven might be. Any hints in terms of general world region?<br /> <br /> I didn't know you were writing an expansion to the Tuatha, but that's awesome, given your personal expertise on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>No hints this time, because a) we talked about it, doesn't mean we're gonna do it (we used to talk about Uganda for a while as well, and that never got off the ground), and b) I've been far too easy on you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T12:42:46-07:00","id":1242458,"title":"","content":"Well, this is certainly exciting nevertheless. So with the Tuatha expansion in mind, have you guys decided that you are in fact willing to expand on existing pantheons, just not create entirely distinct counterparts? I'm asking because there's a couple of pantheons I'm interested in seeing acquire some new members. I'm predicting, due to the huge amount of overlapping cultures being brought together to form it, the official Atua, for instance, aren't going to have all of the laundry list of gods and titans I'd like to see included. I'm predicting that many of the Atua who aren't endemic to Hawaii or New Zealand won't make the cut, and damn it, I want my Makemake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 08-03-2018, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T00:48:24-07:00","id":1242646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1242458#post1242458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is certainly exciting nevertheless. So with the Tuatha expansion in mind, have you guys decided that you are in fact willing to expand on existing pantheons, just not create entirely distinct counterparts? I'm asking because there's a couple of pantheons I'm interested in seeing acquire some new members. I'm predicting, due to the huge amount of overlapping cultures being brought together to form it, the official Atua, for instance, aren't going to have all of the laundry list of gods and titans I'd like to see included. I'm predicting that many of the Atua who aren't endemic to Hawaii or New Zealand won't make the cut, and damn it, I want my Makemake.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I want my Nafanua. And I definitely want to redo all the Pantheons, even though stuff has been generally well-done, even wonderfully-done this time, just because I have my own vision of things and I like to put it out there. We said we won't do anything like that for the moment, and I can't speak for Watcher and his Tuatha and whether he will ever do anything like it for them, but I definitely have my notes ready on some of my babies. We won't do anything like that <i>for the moment</i>, because we don't want to put out any free material that would present an alternative to the official product. Doesn't mean we're never gonna look at the official Pantheons again. When we'll do it, how we'll do it, that's a long way from being decided, since 2e isn't even out yet and we don't want to have any negative effect on their profits. But once 2e is out and running, we <i>will</i> look for ways to come back to redoing the official Pantheons. Ways that are agreeable to Onyx Path and that won't create any issues for anyone, but ways nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T07:57:27-07:00","id":1242719,"title":"","content":"And hey, I want my Havea Hikule'o, so maybe I can have hope! (Though honestly, I've become more and more convinced of the idea of a multiplicity of Polynesian pantheons instead of one the more I've thought and read on it. Even knowing basically nothing on Central Polynesian beliefs, I really do think Hawai'i, Aotearoa, and Western Polynesia could each have a full-fledged pantheon, and that's without mentioning smaller outliers like Rapanui or Niue.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T09:36:22-07:00","id":1242740,"title":"","content":"In your opinion,do the Siunesh Spin of Incarnations to experience the world as mortals less than the other gods do so?Can they do things like drive cars,command armies and advice heroes without being discussed with &quot;the lowly actions&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 08-04-2018, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T10:54:10-07:00","id":1242754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1242740#post1242740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In your opinion,do the Siunesh Spin of Incarnations to experience the world as mortals less than the other gods do so?Can they do things like drive cars,command armies and advice heroes without being discussed with &quot;the lowly actions&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>They could spin off Incarnations if they felt like it, but probably do this <i>incredibly</i> rarely, like, maybe once every thousand years sort of rare. The Shiunesh have a trick where they stand slightly out of phase with reality, allowing them to exist in The World but not be directly affected by Fatebinding issues, but unable to directly interact with The World. So, they don't really need to Incarnate, they are here in The World, wandering around, watching, and interceding when properly called upon.<br /> <br /> They absolutely could advise Heroes, but most of those things are beneath them and they leave to mortals. Armies are commanded by the King of Hatti who is accompanied by the host of War Gods who travel 'out-of-phase' with the king, not by the Gods themselves. Doing stuff for themselves is something they wouldn't be particularly keen on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T11:06:02-07:00","id":1242756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1242754#post1242754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They could spin off Incarnations if they felt like it, but probably do this <i>incredibly</i> rarely, like, maybe once every thousand years sort of rare. The Shiunesh have a trick where they stand slightly out of phase with reality, allowing them to exist in The World but not be directly affected by Fatebinding issues, but unable to directly interact with The World. So, they don't really need to Incarnate, they are here in The World, wandering around, watching, and interceding when properly called upon.<br /> <br /> They absolutely could advise Heroes, but most of those things are beneath them and they leave to mortals. Armies are commanded by the King of Hatti who is accompanied by the host of War Gods who travel 'out-of-phase' with the king, not by the Gods themselves. Doing stuff for themselves is something they wouldn't be particularly keen on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine the Theoi,especially Apollo being like<br /> &quot;Can you believe those guys? I mean i'm fully aware we're jerks,but at least i get of my ass from time to time&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T02:34:17-07:00","id":1296076,"title":"","content":"The whole thing with Sauska and Hedammu sounds like a D&amp;D encounter gone amuck.<br /> <br /> DM: An enormous, terrible, all-consuming, sea monster known as Hedammu emerges. What do you do?<br /> Sauska (The Bard): I will seduce the sea monster!<br /> DM: It's a sea monster. A kaiju. You can't just seduce it.<br /> Sauska: I will transform the entire sea into a love potion and seduce it!<br /> DM:...Fine. Roll for it.<br /> Sauska: (Gets Nat 20.)<br /> DM:...Alright. You seduce the sea monster. (Clasps hands and leans back in chair.) It turns out he's really into vore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T17:15:32-07:00","id":1324580,"title":"","content":"What would be the major differences between Kubaba and her later mantle as Kybele? I assume Kybele would have a higher legend and no longer be considered a minor deity. Are there any major changes to her story and her personality? Would any of her callings or purviews be different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T23:26:22-07:00","id":1324651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1223918-the-\u0161iune\u0161-the-pantheon-of-the-hittite-empire-2e-homebrew?p=1324580#post1324580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the major differences between Kubaba and her later mantle as Kybele? I assume Kybele would have a higher legend and no longer be considered a minor deity. Are there any major changes to her story and her personality? Would any of her callings or purviews be different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kybele is a super difficult case that I don't really know what to do with yet. Her &quot;home&quot; Pantheon, the Phrygians, are too ill-attested to deal with in detail. Most of what we know even about Kybele comes from the Greeks, who however already conflate her with Rhea. Then there's the straight line of development from Kubaba. It's really difficult to flesh out Kybele as a distinct character between all of this - I mean, she definitely <i>is</i> one, but I can't really get to her. So yeah, there is a completely different deity to be found in Kybele, one much more strongly associated with fury and castration, but I can't really describe her clearly at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}